  "summary": "The Toledo Blade editorial board praises Toledo City Council's decision to renew a $14,000 Flock ALPR contract with the police department, arguing the cameras help solve crimes and that privacy concerns are overblown compared to cell phone and internet tracking. The editorial notes Cleveland and Dayton have banished Flock cameras and that four Toledo councilmembers voted no.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "Toledo City Council agonized over an easy and obvious decision but finally made the correct choice and renewed the police department contract with Flock Group Inc. for cameras that read and record license plates.",
      "paragraph_idx": 0
    },
    {
      "quote": "Cleveland and Dayton have both banished Flock cameras over concerns about a surveillance state.",
      "paragraph_idx": 2
    },
    {
      "quote": "Being recorded by a Flock camera set up in a specific Toledo location is much less intrusive than the constant monitoring required to provide cell phone service",
      "paragraph_idx": 4
    }
  ],
